id: crush
name: Crush

Add llm.birks.dev as an OpenAI-compatible provider in Crush.

--- file ~/.config/crush/crush.json (json) ---
{
  "$schema": "https://charm.land/crush.json",
  "providers": {
    "llm-birks-dev": {
      "type": "openai-compat",
      "base_url": "https://llm.birks.dev/v1",
      "api_key": "$LLM_BIRKS_DEV_API_KEY",
      "models": [
        {
          "id": "Qwen3-Coder-30B",
          "name": "Qwen3-Coder-30B"
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}

--- commands (bash) ---
export LLM_BIRKS_DEV_API_KEY="YOUR_API_KEY"

crush

--- notes ---
- The $LLM_BIRKS_DEV_API_KEY form tells Crush to expand the value from your environment.
- The openai-compat provider type sends Authorization: Bearer, which is what the gateway expects.
- Crush also supports an anthropic provider type; the OpenAI-compatible route is the tested one here.

--- agent prompt ---
Configure Crush on this machine to use my self-hosted llm.birks.dev endpoint at https://llm.birks.dev. Add an openai-compat provider to my Crush config that expands the API key from an environment variable. Use the model "Qwen3-Coder-30B". Read the API key from the LLM_BIRKS_DEV_API_KEY environment variable. Do not write the key itself into any file in a git repository, and do not print it. Preserve my existing unrelated configuration.
